00:42:51.000 --> 00:42:51.880
It is.
确实是。

910
00:42:52.080 --> 00:42:52.480
Thank you.
谢谢你。

911
00:42:52.480 --> 00:42:54.520
Way to bring it full circle, lady.
圆得真漂亮，这位女士。

912
00:42:54.940 --> 00:42:55.640
All right.
好啦。

913
00:42:55.820 --> 00:42:57.500
This is from Louise F.
这封信来自苏格兰的

914
00:42:57.760 --> 00:42:59.340
from Scotland, who said,
路易丝·F，她说，

915
00:42:59.560 --> 00:43:00.460
Hey, office ladies.
嘿，办公室女士们。

916
00:43:00.680 --> 00:43:06.100
I have always wondered, what would happen if someone was the main focus of an episode one week,
我一直很好奇，如果某个人是一周某集的主要焦点，

917
00:43:06.140 --> 00:43:09.800
but when it came to filming, they were so ill that they couldn't come to set?
但在拍摄时，他们病得太重而无法来到片场，会发生什么呢？

918
00:43:10.020 --> 00:43:13.220
Would the episode be rewritten or filmed a different week?
这集会被重写，还是会在另一周拍摄？

919
00:43:13.680 --> 00:43:18.240
Surely, with the amount of episodes you guys filmed, this was bound to happen at some point.
当然，考虑到你们拍摄的剧集数量，这在某种程度上是不可避免的。

920
00:43:19.400 --> 00:43:20.180
Oh, Louise.
噢，路易丝。

921
00:43:20.500 --> 00:43:21.160
Oh, Louise.
噢，路易丝。

922
00:43:21.160 --> 00:43:23.540
Louise, Louise, first of all, hi from Scotland.
路易丝，路易丝，首先，来自苏格兰的问候。

923
00:43:23.540 --> 00:43:24.600
I love Scotland.
我爱苏格兰。

924
00:43:24.940 --> 00:43:25.220
Yes.
没错。

925
00:43:25.580 --> 00:43:25.740
Okay.
好的。

926
00:43:25.800 --> 00:43:26.740
I just had to say that.
我只是得说这个。

927
00:43:26.820 --> 00:43:27.120
Okay.
好吧。

928
00:43:27.360 --> 00:43:28.680
Because I went there for my honeymoon.
因为我度蜜月时去过那里。

929
00:43:28.800 --> 00:43:29.740
You know how much I love Scotland.
你知道我多爱苏格兰。

930
00:43:30.060 --> 00:43:30.380
Okay.
好啦。

931
00:43:30.920 --> 00:43:31.820
Now I'm going to focus.
现在我要集中注意力了。

932
00:43:32.200 --> 00:43:32.520
Yes.
是的。

933
00:43:33.540 --> 00:43:35.000
So here's the thing.
所以情况是这样的。

934
00:43:35.320 --> 00:43:40.060
We had to just go to work anyway, basically, is the short answer.
简短的回答是，基本上我们无论如何都得去上班。

935
00:43:40.060 --> 00:43:49.740
There are so many moving parts and so many people involved in pulling an episode together that if it was written and planned and there was a shoot schedule,
筹备一集节目需要协调的环节和人员实在太多了，如果剧本已经写好、计划好并且有了拍摄日程，

936
00:43:50.040 --> 00:43:52.040
it was very hard to undo that.
要推翻它是非常困难的。

937
00:43:52.040 --> 00:43:55.360
And yes, every once in a while it happened.
是的，这种事偶尔确实会发生。

938
00:43:55.360 --> 00:44:07.120
Like, if someone was truly too sick to come to set, we might rearrange some of the week's schedule to give them an afternoon off or a morning off or maybe the whole day off.
比如，如果有人病得实在太重无法来片场，我们可能会重新调整当周的日程，给他们放个下午假、早上的假，或者干脆放假一天。

939
00:44:07.120 --> 00:44:09.800
But it was very difficult and very rare.
但这非常困难，也非常罕见。

940
00:44:09.920 --> 00:44:10.860
It was very rare.
真的非常罕见。

941
00:44:10.860 --> 00:44:19.900
They would try to, like Jenna said, move the schedule so maybe you could go home early, you know, pull up someone else's talking heads, things like that.
就像珍娜说的，他们会尽量调整日程，也许能让你早点回家，你知道的，把其他人的单人采访提前，诸如此类。

942
00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:22.240
But mostly we just muscled through it.
但大多数时候，我们都只能咬牙挺过去。

943
00:44:22.760 --> 00:44:31.440
The only time I remember us doing a big switcheroo was Dwight's speech because Rain was so, so sick.
我记得我们唯一一次做重大调整是在拍《德怀特的演讲》时，因为雷恩病得太重太重了。

944
00:44:31.440 --> 00:44:33.640
And he was the focus of that episode.
而且他正是那一集的焦点。

945
00:44:33.640 --> 00:44:33.820
Yeah.
对。

946
00:44:33.940 --> 00:44:35.920
And we had to film at that hotel.
而且我们必须在那家酒店拍摄。

947
00:44:36.020 --> 00:44:41.780
And that was one time I remember I got a call from our AD and they were like, okay, the hotel has been canceled.
那是少数几次我记得接到副导演电话，他们说，好吧，酒店的拍摄取消了。

948
00:44:41.980 --> 00:44:42.980
We're moving things around.
我们要调换一下日程。

949
00:44:43.700 --> 00:44:45.060
Rain's going to the doctor.
雷恩要去医院看医生。

950
00:44:45.200 --> 00:44:45.860
He's too sick.
他病得太厉害了。

951
00:44:46.060 --> 00:44:46.280
Yeah.
对。

952
00:44:46.500 --> 00:44:50.900
But really, I mean, you could probably count on one hand the number of times that happened.
但说真的，我的意思是，这种情况发生的次数大概一只手都数得过来。

953
00:44:51.380 --> 00:44:51.780
Yeah.
对。

954
00:44:52.060 --> 00:44:56.920
There were sometimes like life events, like a death in the family.
有时候会遇到一些生活大事，比如家里有人去世。

955
00:44:57.160 --> 00:44:57.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

956
00:44:57.600 --> 00:45:05.360
And I remember we made space for people, obviously, to go grieve and be with their families.
我记得我们当然会腾出时间让大家去哀悼、去陪伴家人。

957
00:45:06.400 --> 00:45:10.220
But if someone was sick, you had to kind of just power through.
但如果有人生病了，你基本上就得硬挺过去。

958
00:45:10.540 --> 00:45:13.600
I mean, I had false labor and went to work the next day.
我是说，我假宫缩过，第二天照样去上班。

959
00:45:14.500 --> 00:45:16.560
I was in the hospital and they called.
我当时在医院，他们还打电话来。

960
00:45:16.900 --> 00:45:17.140
Remember?
记得吗？

961
00:45:17.360 --> 00:45:19.420
Ken Svornack was like, Angela, are we having this baby tonight?
肯·斯沃纳克（Ken Svornack）当时说：“安吉拉，我们今晚要生孩子吗？”

962
00:45:19.620 --> 00:45:23.740
Because it was the next day where Andy proposes and the Ferris wheel and all that.
因为第二天就是安迪求婚、摩天轮和所有那些戏份。

963
00:45:23.920 --> 00:45:25.600
And I was like, I'll let you know.
我说：“我随时向你汇报。”

964
00:45:25.880 --> 00:45:27.240
I totally remember that.
我完全记得那件事。

965
00:45:27.240 --> 00:45:29.680
And listen, this is not exclusive to The Office.
而且听着，这不仅仅是《办公室》这部剧独有的。

966
00:45:29.760 --> 00:45:30.220
No, no, no.
对，对，对。

967
00:45:30.340 --> 00:45:31.680
This is the entertainment industry.
这就是整个娱乐行业。

968
00:45:32.080 --> 00:45:35.180
When I did the movie Walk Hard, John C.
当年我拍电影《永不退缩》时，约翰·C·

969
00:45:35.220 --> 00:45:37.080
Reilly got really sick.
赖利（John C. Reilly）病得很重。

970
00:45:37.300 --> 00:45:40.280
I think he had like a strep throat or something.
我想他好像得了链球菌性咽喉炎什么的。

971
00:45:40.340 --> 00:45:44.200
And we had to do like a whole makeout scene anyway.
但我们无论如何还是得拍一场完整的吻戏。

972
00:45:45.020 --> 00:45:50.540
And then I got sick and I got so sick that I lost my voice.
然后我也病了，病得很重，甚至失声了。

973
00:45:50.660 --> 00:45:51.660
I had laryngitis.
我得了喉炎。

974
00:45:51.820 --> 00:45:53.060
I couldn't speak.
我说不出话来。

975
00:45:53.240 --> 00:45:54.780
And I was really sick.
我病得真的很厉害。

976
00:45:54.780 --> 00:45:57.120
And they were like, you still have to come to work.
结果他们说：“你还是得来上班。”

977
00:45:57.220 --> 00:45:57.920
I'm like, how?
我说：“怎么去？”

978
00:45:58.400 --> 00:45:58.860
How?
怎么去？

979
00:45:59.080 --> 00:46:00.300
I can't speak.
我都说不了话。

980
00:46:00.560 --> 00:46:03.840
They're like, we're going to shoot some stuff where you're not talking today.
他们说：“我们今天拍一些你不用说话的镜头就行了。”

981
00:46:04.460 --> 00:46:07.460
I mean, it's like you're going to just show up.
我的意思是，就好像你必须得露面一样。

982
00:46:07.640 --> 00:46:09.040
It is pretty bonkers.
这确实挺离谱的。

983
00:46:09.040 --> 00:46:09.960
It is.
确实。

984
00:46:10.100 --> 00:46:14.640
And we're kind of laughing because I think in hindsight, sometimes you look back at those
我们在笑是因为我觉得事后回想起来，有时候你看着那些

985
00:46:14.640 --> 00:46:15.560
moments, you're like, what?
时刻，会想：什么鬼？

986
00:46:15.700 --> 00:46:20.440
But it does involve so many moving parts and so many people that they are just constantly
但因为其中包含太多运转的环节和太多的人，他们总是在

987
00:46:21.000 --> 00:46:25.160
trying to make sure they make their day and get something shot because they have a limited
努力确保能赶上进度、拍完镜头，因为他们有着有限的

988
00:46:25.160 --> 00:46:26.460
time and a limited budget.
时间和有限的预算。

989
00:46:26.460 --> 00:46:27.080
Yes.
是的。

990
00:46:27.380 --> 00:46:31.320
And there is like this element of the show must go on.
而且确实有一种“演出必须继续”的成分。

991
00:46:31.460 --> 00:46:34.460
And that's been a part of, you know, actors.
这也是你知道的，演员的一部分。

992
00:46:34.960 --> 00:46:35.060
Yes.
是的。

993
00:46:35.560 --> 00:46:38.160
For all time, the show must go on.
一直以来，演出必须继续。

994
00:46:38.380 --> 00:46:42.840
And there is that spirit when you're making a movie or you're making a TV show.
当你拍电影或拍电视剧时，确实有那种精神。

995
00:46:43.160 --> 00:46:48.680
And I think I famously told the story of how incredibly sick I was one week at the office
我想我曾出名地讲过那个故事：在办公室的那一周我病得有多厉害，

996
00:46:48.680 --> 00:46:51.660
and I took a bunch of Sudafed.
我吃了一堆伪麻黄碱。

997
00:46:51.960 --> 00:46:52.380
Yes.
是的。

998
00:46:52.520 --> 00:46:53.500
So I could make it through.
好让我能撑过去。

999
00:46:53.920 --> 00:46:56.680
And didn't Greg say it was one of your best performances?
而且格雷格不是说那是你最好的表演之一吗？

1000
00:46:57.060 --> 00:46:57.440
Greg.
格雷格。

1001
00:46:57.760 --> 00:46:59.160
Like reach out to your agent or something?
比如联系你的经纪人或者别的什么？

1002
00:46:59.420 --> 00:47:03.440
He called my manager and was like, Jenna was incredible today.
他给我的经纪人打电话说，珍娜今天表现太棒了。

1003
00:47:03.840 --> 00:47:04.360
Incredible.
太棒了。

1004
00:47:04.800 --> 00:47:07.420
You're like, I was super Sudafed it up.
你当时就想，我当时吃了超级多的伪麻黄碱。

1005
00:47:07.660 --> 00:47:08.020
Exactly.
没错。

1006
00:47:08.020 --> 00:47:10.400
I'm like, oh, I don't know what that says.
我就想，哦，我不知道这说明了什么。

1007
00:47:10.540 --> 00:47:12.540
But anyway, thank you for that question.
不过无论如何，谢谢你提出这个问题。

1008
00:47:13.140 --> 00:47:13.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1009
00:47:13.700 --> 00:47:14.300
We juSt.
我们只是。

1010
00:47:14.460 --> 00:47:16.040
We just powered through.
我们只是硬着头皮坚持了下来。

1011
00:47:16.260 --> 00:47:16.620
We did.
我们确实做到了。

1012
00:47:17.120 --> 00:47:19.800
Well, everyone, this was such a fun episode.
好了，各位，这真是一期非常有趣的节目。

1013
00:47:20.140 --> 00:47:21.220
Thank you so much for listening.
非常感谢大家的收听。

1014
00:47:21.480 --> 00:47:26.080
I want to give a special thank you to Holiday Reinhorn for sharing her story about the origin
我要特别感谢霍莉·雷恩霍恩分享了关于德怀特那件衬衫来源的故事

1015
00:47:26.080 --> 00:47:27.800
of Dwight's button down shirt.
。

1016
00:47:28.020 --> 00:47:28.440
Amazing.
太惊艳了。

1017
00:47:29.140 --> 00:47:33.300
And of course, you guys, I'll put links in our stories where you can check out the amazing
当然啦，各位，我会在我们的快拍里放上链接，大家可以去了解那个由雷恩和霍莉倾注了大量心血和时间的精彩

1018
00:47:33.300 --> 00:47:38.040
organization that Rain and Holly have put so much of their heart and time into Lede Haiti.
组织——莱代海地（Lede Haiti）。

1019
00:47:38.840 --> 00:47:45.940
And thank you to, oh my goodness, the amazing Christy D from Wheeling, West Virginia, who sent
还要感谢，天哪，来自西弗吉尼亚州惠灵的了不起的克里斯蒂·D，她寄来了

1020
00:47:45.940 --> 00:47:47.700
in the Diaries of the Mustard shirt.
《芥末衬衫日记》。

1021
00:47:48.120 --> 00:47:49.140
What a delight.
真是太让人高兴了。

1022
00:47:49.360 --> 00:47:51.340
Talk about a dainty delight was reading that.
读到这个简直就是一种精致的享受。

1023
00:47:51.560 --> 00:47:53.840
Thank you for inspiring this episode, Christy.
谢谢你启发了这一期节目，克里斯蒂。

1024
00:47:54.240 --> 00:47:56.300
We'll see you guys all next week.
我们下周同一时间再见。

1025
00:47:56.480 --> 00:47:56.980
See you then.
到时见。

1026
00:47:57.140 --> 00:48:01.430
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1027
00:48:01.770 --> 00:48:06.810
Office Ladies is a presentation of Odyssey and is produced by Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》是奥德赛（Audyssey）出品的节目，由珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金西制作。

